@title STORY • JORDAN: TEN BREAKUPS
@bg dorm_room_night
You're Jordan Ellis. Midfielder. Philly. Bi, out since you were fifteen, and currently on breakup number ten with Brooke Anderson.
Your phone: Brooke. "u up"
It's 1:14 a.m. It's always 1:14 a.m.
> [Bold] "no. go to sleep brooke." -> a1
> [Sweet] "yeah. what's wrong?" -> a2
> [Good] Turn your phone off. -> a3
*a1
@add Self 2
Brooke: "ok."
Brooke: "goodnight jordy"
She hasn't called you Jordy since breakup number four. You stare at it for an hour.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Brooke 2
She calls. She's crying. Her parents called again. Scottsdale. "Disappointed." You talk till 3 a.m. Like nothing ever broke.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Self 3
You sleep. For real. Eight hours. You wake up feeling like a person.
*a_done
@bg soccer_pitch_day
@show nicole
Nicole: Ellis. Your passes are sloppy. Is this about Brooke again?
> [Bitchy] "Is everything about Brooke to you, Nicole?" -> b1
> [Good] "...Yeah. It is. I'll fix it." -> b2
*b1
@add Nicole_Beef 2
Nicole: When you play like this? Yeah.
She's not wrong. You hate when she's not wrong.
@jump end
*b2
@add Nicole_Bond 3
Nicole: (surprised) Okay. Thanks for being honest. That's... actually really captain-y of you.
Jordan: Don't make it weird.
*end
Jordan Ellis loves hard and fights harder. This year, she's figuring out the difference between loving someone and not being able to let go.
